  "decision_reasons": [
    "Main-seed total throughput changes by +0.06%, second seed -0.55%, custom bounds -2.01%, direct stem -3.04%. Paired median ratios are 0.994, 1.000, 1.034, 1.044, respectively; custom wins only 8/20 and direct 7/20.",
    "Main p95 increases from 1420 to 1479 ms, custom p95 from 2303 to 2376 ms, and second-seed maximum from 2006 to 2548 ms. These results are retained and do not justify production selection.",
    "The unaffected Overworld control shows -1.78% aggregate throughput and p95 increase from 852 to 909 ms. External activity limits attribution; it does not establish that Nether regressions are harmless.",
    "Synthetic nine/thirteen-run lookups are substantially faster in isolation, but the complete workload does not improve. Construction, larger objects and other work remain possible offsets; their separate costs are not established.",
    "Every measured Nether lookup uses the index and all read/run-shape counters exactly match C58. The added joined metadata is 24.9\u201327.2 MB/region; process peaks vary and cannot prove lower memory or a sustained bound."
  ],
  "next_investigation": "Read-only resource attribution of the unchanged C58 library is complete: 61,440 chunks match original and C58. Nether needs 4.3\u20134.5 CPU-seconds/region versus 1.2 for Overworld; both average around 3 CPU-seconds per elapsed second under recorded host activity. Next measure per-root queue, enumeration, anchor evaluation, publication, process CPU deltas and worker intervals for dispatched anchor tasks. Distinguish blocked/preempted workers from a long final task or insufficient available parallel work. Keep 16 configured workers; do not substitute thread-count tuning.",
  "limitations": [
    "Final uncontended timing, no-regression and subsecond confirmation remain deferred by user.",
    "No extra concurrent/lifecycle acceptance suite is run for this unselected prototype; output parity alone is not acceptance.",
    "Joined metadata excludes transient allocations and other engine/global state. Whole-process peak includes startup/warmups and excludes later NBT comparisons.",
    "Synthetic microbenchmarks exclude construction, real access locality, production object layout/ownership, scheduling and most generation work. They cannot be converted into whole-region savings.",
    "Prior C53 worker-stack reclassification is evidence for further measurement only, not a scheduler diagnosis or summed wall time."
  ],
